   "name": "Naming binary compounds",
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Name the metal first with its element name. Then name the non-metal with the ending -ide: oxygen becomes oxide, chlorine becomes chloride. For metals with more than one valence, write the valence in Roman numerals: FeCl₃ is iron (III) chloride."
    }
   },
